  "solution": {
    "text": "Given numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>153,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>155</mn></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>155</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></math><br />Total number of ways <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>78</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3003</mn></math><br />The numbers which are multiple of <math><mn>5</mn></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>15,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>155</mn></math><br /><math><mn>155</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></math><br />The number of ways in which product is a multiple of <math><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo></math> (Both two numbers from <math><mn>5,15,25</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>155</mn></math> ) or (one number from <math><mn>5,15,25</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>145</mn></math> and one number from the remaining numbers).<br /><math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow>